<article class="env-lemma" id="01XC">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01XC">Lemma <span data-tag="01XC">30.2.3</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to S$ be a morphism of schemes. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module. If $f$ is affine then $R^ if_*\mathcal{F} = 0$ for all $i > 0$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      According to Cohomology, Lemma <a href="/tag/01E4" data-tag="01E4">20.7.3</a> the sheaf $R^ if_*\mathcal{F}$ is the sheaf associated to the presheaf $V \mapsto H^ i(f^{-1}(V), \mathcal{F}|_{f^{-1}(V)})$. By assumption, whenever $V$ is affine we have that $f^{-1}(V)$ is affine, see Morphisms, Definition <a href="/tag/01S6" data-tag="01S6">29.11.1</a>. By Lemma <a href="/tag/01XB" data-tag="01XB">30.2.2</a> we conclude that $H^ i(f^{-1}(V), \mathcal{F}|_{f^{-1}(V)}) = 0$ whenever $V$ is affine. Since $S$ has a basis consisting of affine opens we win. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>